{"thought":"The `--at` option is still not being recognized, even without any help text. This indicates that the issue is likely related to how the Click library is handling the option itself or the completion process. I will create a very simple command with just the `--at` option and no additional parameters to see if it can be recognized at all. This will help confirm if the problem lies with the option definition or the completion system.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import pytest
import click


def _get_completions(cli, args, incomplete):
    from click.shell_completion import ShellComplete
    comp = ShellComplete(cli, {}, cli.name, "_CLICK_COMPLETE")
    return comp.get_completions(args, incomplete)


def test_simple_option_recognition():
    @click.command()
    @click.option("--at")
    def cli(at):
        pass

    # Check if the --at option is recognized
    try:
        completions = _get_completions(cli, ["--at"], "")
        assert completions is not None
        assert any(c.value == '--at' for c in completions)
    except Exception as e:
        pytest.fail(f"Completion raised an exception: {e}")"}}
